{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A son is born to Naomi.</b> Like ויהי לה לבן (and he became a son to her)." "<b>The father of David.</b> It is possible that it refers back to Jesse and also to Obed, like אלהי אבי אברהם ואלהי אבי יצחק (the God of my father Abraham and the God of my father Isaac). By reasoning, since Nahshon died in the wilderness — for it is impossible that he was a youth yet a banner-leader journeying at the head of Israel. Furthermore, Scripture would have mentioned him as one who entered the land, and there would not be another prince of the tribe. Now between one who entered the land until David was born there are only 366 years, for Scripture says: ויהי בשמונים שנה וארבע מאות שנה היא השנה הרביעית למלך שלמה (and it came to pass in the eightieth year and four hundredth year, which is the fourth year of King Solomon's reign). And David lived seventy years. And the children of Israel journeyed in the wilderness forty years. And if we say that Salmon was one year old when he entered the land, then there are four — Salmon and Boaz and Obed and Jesse — so each fathered when he was ninety-one years old. And if a disputant arises and says that Nahshon was less than twenty years old when he went out from Egypt, then it may be reckoned that he was eighteen, and we do not subtract the years of Israel's going in the wilderness. Then there will be five, and each will have fathered when he was eighty-four, and this is correct in my eyes. For Boaz was old, as we learn from the fact that he said to Ruth not to go after the young men; and Jesse was old when he fathered David, for he is eighth among his sons. And it is possible that he was named Obed, because he was born to an old man, and he did not take a wife except for the honor of the Name. And also the mother abandoned her faith and her native land, and sought refuge under the wing of HaShem; therefore the son will be one who serves HaShem, for most sons resemble their father and mother, for they are the roots."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:41.458390993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}